    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d988">

                <pb facs="1003" n="883" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg883"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August 14,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 877.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith for your information a
                    copy of a letter from Mr. J. B. Hammond,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d988-f1"/> in
                    regard to 19 typewriting machines shipped by him to Messrs. Bond, Seller &amp;
                    Co., of Constantinople, Turkey, which have been detained in the
                    custom-house.</p>
                <pb facs="1004" n="884" xml:id="pg884"/>
                <p>You are requested to give this matter your attention and advise the Department of
                    the result.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
